2026-11-21T12:45:46 | Claude chunk logs-investigation | found | Q1: logging works live. The dist exe (pid 15552) writes run-20261121-112716-15552.log line by line (AutoFlush, AppLog.cs:115): it really held 7,853 then 8,518 bytes a minute apart, but the directory listing showed 5,801 bytes / 11:28:54 (NTFS updates the size and time it lists lazily for a file another process holds open). Repro on the hidden desktop: same thing. Also: the console sink is off for an exe started from a shortcut (no stdout handle), --mcp never inits logging, and clicking around in the UI writes almost no lines.
2026-11-21T12:46:41 | Claude chunk logs-investigation | done | Investigation only; no code or openspec changes.\n\nQ1, logs "not appearing while it runs". The file sink works live. AppLog.cs:115 opens the file with AutoFlush=true and FileShare.ReadWrite, so every line reaches the disk at once. The dist exe 15552 contains AppLog (run-20261121-112716-15552.log). The file held 7,853 and then 8,518 bytes a minute apart, but the folder listing (Explorer, dir) showed 5,801 bytes / 11:28:54. NTFS updates the size and time it lists lazily for a file another process holds open. A hidden-desktop repro with the Debug build showed the same lag (the listing said 1,118, the file held 1,972).\nOther reasons it looks empty:\n(1) The console sink needs a stdout handle (AppLog.HasConsole, Program.cs:27), and a WinExe started from the shortcut or Explorer has none. Only dotnet run shows lines in a terminal.\n(2) The UI barely logs: 5 clicks wrote 0 lines, and 11:36 to 12:36 is empty. The lines are mostly ModelContextProtocol chatter (4 per tool call, not covered by the "Microsoft" filter at AppLog.cs:122).\n(3) The --mcp relay (Program.cs:24) never calls Init and writes only stderr.\n(4) The version in the log header is wrong for dist. Paths.cs:23 takes the newest loose TaskManager*.dll in BaseDirectory, and dist\\ still holds stale 31 Oct dlls next to the single-file exe, so every dist build reports +20261031003042.\nRetention is safe: Prune skips the current file, and a delete of another running instance's open file fails without harm.\n\nQ2, crashes. "No process crash on 20-21 Nov" still stands: no APPCRASH, no .NET Runtime 1026 for TaskManager*, no dumps after 11 Nov, no msedgewebview2 entries in 14 days. Every run log without a clean-exit line has a marker entry. But the owner did see the window freeze or vanish 4 times: hangs 9604 (20 Nov 05:11) and 23852 (09:03, closed by Windows), and kills 22564 (12:02, publish) and 44828 (21 Nov 06:27, agent). The app itself logs each of these as "ERROR Crash: ... a crash in native code or a kill". That message is why it reads as a crash.\nNot caught:\n- hangs: nothing at all\n- kills and OS restarts: labelled as a crash\n- TaskScheduler.UnobservedTaskException: not hooked\n- Photino Dispatcher.UnhandledException: no subscriber, so exceptions are swallowed silently\n- Blazor render exceptions: WebViewRenderer.HandleException only notifies JS, no ILogger reaches AppLog, and index.html has no #blazor-error-ui\n- JS errors, WebView2 ProcessFailed: not hooked\n- native AV, stack overflow, FailFast: only the marker at the next start\n- anything thrown before Program.cs:56: no crash line\nCaught: AppDomain unhandled exceptions after line 56 (timers, threads, async void, reverse-P/Invoke callbacks) and the explicit LogCrash sites.\nFixes:\n- a UI-thread watchdog that logs and dumps stacks after 30 s\n- hook UnobservedTaskException, Dispatcher.UnhandledException and an ErrorBoundary that log\n- route the Blazor builder's logging to AppLog\n- hook CoreWebView2.ProcessFailed plus a window.onerror/unhandledrejection bridge\n- record the exit kind (session end, publish stop) and word it "did not exit cleanly"\n- log ui.command for every command\n- fix the version stamp, and clear the stale dist files.
